<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30155" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūtātōrĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		mutator, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			changing</i> or <i>exchanging</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indumentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 56</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūtātōrĭ-um</span></b> ,
				i, n.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A cape, tippet, wimple, change of raiment;</i> Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναβόλαιον</span>,
					<i><span class="en">Hier. in Isa. 3, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Isa. 3,
				22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Zech. 3, 4
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Mutatorium Caesaris, perh. <i>a house of
			accommodation</i> or <i>a pleasure-house</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Gud. 199, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
